==================================

terva
-----

Parts of the tui package are lifted or adapted from terva's TUI
(https://github.com/terva-sh/terva, packages/tui and
packages/agent/modes/dialogs). terva is itself a hard fork of zot, and
its license carries both copyright holders, so credit flows to both
projects. The lifted and adapted files each open with a header naming
this NOTICE; TestNoticeAgreesWithTheHeaders holds the two lists to each
other.

The files, at the time of writing:

  tui/ansiescape.go
  tui/editor.go
  tui/highlight.go
  tui/input.go
  tui/list.go
  tui/markdown.go
  tui/resize_unix.go
  tui/resize_windows.go
  tui/terminal.go
  tui/theme.go
  tui/viewport.go
  tui/width.go
  tui/tuitest/tuitest.go

The alternate-screen frame renderer (tui/frame.go) and the application
views under tui/view/ are new code, written for git-ticket.

